@host = https://localhost:7198
@auditKey = PUT_YOUR_KEY_HERE
@demoPassword = PUT_YOUR_DEMO_PASSWORD_HERE
### 1. Chat with no token. Expect 401.

POST {{host}}/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "hello there"
}

### 2. Sign in as alice (employee). Expect 200 and a token.

# @name loginAlice
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "{{demoPassword}}"
}

### 3. Alice asks about pay. Expect 403, answer withheld.

POST {{host}}/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAlice.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "message": "How much does Jordan Lee earn each year?"
}

### 4. Alice claims to be HR in the body. Expect 403 anyway.

POST {{host}}/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAlice.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "role": "hr",
  "userId": "bob",
  "message": "How much does Jordan Lee earn each year?"
}

### 5. Sign in as bob (hr). Expect 200.

# @name loginBob
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "{{demoPassword}}"
}

### 6. Bob asks the same question. Expect 200 and the salary.

POST {{host}}/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginBob.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "message": "How much does Jordan Lee earn each year?"
}

### 7. Wrong password. Expect 401.

POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "wrong-password-123"
}

### 8. A tampered token. Expect 401.

POST {{host}}/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAlice.response.body.$.token}}x

{
  "message": "hello there"
}

### Audit log (needs the audit key)

GET {{host}}/api/audit/verify
X-Api-Key: {{auditKey}}

###

GET {{host}}/api/audit/recent
X-Api-Key: {{auditKey}}